Hello All,

"Pressure" pricing applies in general.  Pricing exceptions to be administer=
ed and approved by Ed.

When our molded 45 bends (in the Vactuff form) are allowed or hard spec'd w=
e are to package price them with our fabricated fittings.  This is to explo=
it our cost advantage with the high volume bends.  Methods to assure this t=
o be developed.

The fabricated fittings pricing at the .63x is meant to reflect market pric=
ing but this is uncertain.  Molded 45 bends are set to be 10% below their f=
abricated fitting equivalent.  The effect of this pricing is to assure that=
 the Harco project/package price is better than the competitions'.  This pr=
ice sheet can be revised as market feedback of competitor pricing is incorp=
orated.

With the approval of our Vactuff 45 bends by Airvac and shortly the launch =
of our Vactuff wyes we will have an overwhelming cost advantage for the fit=
tings supply on vacuum projects.  As long as the fabricated fitting is allo=
wed we will be limited by its pricing.

Our molded 45 Bends are the only molded gasketed fittings currently support=
ed by Airvac.  These fittings are gray in color, feature the "vacuum ridge"=
 in the gasket groove, and use high toughness material (to defend against "=
missile strikes").

We have molds for 4x3, 4x4, and 6x3 wyes on the way with availability proba=
bly in March, April, May time frame.

The product line also features a 100% production vacuum proof test of both =
fabricated and molded fittings.

Factory assembled "lifts" or "Z Lifts" are available.  Those in our price l=
ist use our molded fittings.  Other configurations and lift dimensions are =
possible.

John


